1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,270
Why is this AI chip
这块AI芯片，

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:02,770
the size of a dinner plate?
为什么有餐盘那么大？

3
00:00:02,770 --> 00:00:04,230
Line up fifty nine of them,
排上59块，

4
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:06,660
and they run a three trillion parameter AI.
就能跑一个三万亿参数的AI。

5
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,840
Cerebras says it can write up to two thousand tokens a second.
Cerebras说，一秒能吐上千到两千个词元，

6
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,750
That's pages of text, every second.
差不多每秒好几页字。

7
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:12,670
Today's question:
今天的问题：

8
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,860
why does a bigger chip make AI faster?
芯片做大，AI为什么就变快？

9
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,520
Meet Chippy.
认识一下小芯，

10
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,220
A normal chip, about as big as a postage stamp.
一块普通芯片，跟邮票差不多大。

11
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,990
Chippy does math insanely fast.
小芯算数快得吓人，

12
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:22,280
Trillions of multiplications a second.
一秒几万亿次乘法。

13
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,330
But here's the catch:
可问题是：

14
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:25,250
most of the time, Chippy is waiting.
小芯大部分时间在等。

15
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:26,080
Waiting for what?
等什么？

16
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,860
For numbers to arrive from memory.
等内存把数字送过来。

17
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,900
Picture a chef who cooks in one second,
想象一个厨师，一秒就能炒好菜，

18
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,690
but the fridge is down the hall.
可冰箱在走廊尽头。

19
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:33,600
To write each word, an AI must read
AI每写一个词，

20
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,840
a huge pile of its numbers from memory.
都要把一大堆参数从内存读一遍。

21
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,440
It's like running to the fridge
就像每做一道菜，

22
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,360
for every ingredient of every dish.
每样食材都得跑一趟冰箱。

23
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,280
So the speed limit isn't the cooking.
所以限速的不是炒菜，

24
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,280
It's the walking.
是走路。

25
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,050
Engineers have a name for this:
这个问题有个名字：

26
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:45,080
the memory wall.
内存墙。

27
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,990
For years, chips got faster at math
这些年芯片算得越来越快，

28
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:49,410
much faster than memory got at delivering.
内存送货却跟不上。

29
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:49,870
Twist one:
反转一：

30
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:52,010
what if the fridge sat right on the counter?
要是冰箱就在灶台边呢？

31
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,430
That's the Cerebras idea:
这就是Cerebras的思路：

32
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:56,160
don't cut the silicon wafer into little chips.
硅晶圆不切成小芯片。

33
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,320
Keep the whole wafer:
整片留着，

34
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:00,270
one giant chip, about twenty centimeters on a side.
一块巨大的芯片，边长二十多厘米。

35
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:02,660
Memory sits right beside every tiny core.
内存就贴在每个小核旁边，

36
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,770
Forty four gigabytes on one wafer.
一片晶圆上有44个G。

37
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:06,940
The ingredients are within arm's reach.
食材就在手边，

38
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:07,960
No more hallway.
不用走廊了。

39
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:08,470
Twist two:
反转二：

40
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:10,630
forty four gigabytes still isn't enough.
44个G还是不够。

41
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:12,170
Even at four bits per number,
每个参数用4个比特存，

42
00:01:12,170 --> 00:01:14,830
the model weighs about one and a half terabytes.
整个模型也有大约1.5个T。

43
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:16,850
That's about sixteen gigabytes per layer,
一层大约16个G，

44
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:18,650
and there are ninety three layers.
一共93层。

45
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:20,140
So build an assembly line:
那就搭一条流水线：

46
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:22,270
each wafer holds one or two layers.
每片晶圆管一两层。

47
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:23,780
Wafer one runs its layers,
第一片算完自己的层，

48
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:25,940
then hands the result to wafer two.
把结果交给第二片。

49
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:28,320
Only small results travel between wafers.
晶圆之间只传小小的中间结果，

50
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,130
The heavy numbers never move.
沉重的参数一动不动。

51
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:32,180
Each hop takes about two microseconds.
每传一次大约两微秒，

52
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:34,530
One blink fits tens of thousands of hops.
眨一下眼，够传几万次。

53
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:36,520
If the heavy numbers had to travel too,
要是参数也得搬来搬去，

54
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,380
we'd be right back in the hallway.
那就又回到走廊了。

55
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,870
Twist three, the sneaky one:
反转三，最鸡贼的一个：

56
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:43,020
while wafer two works, wafer one starts the next request.
第二片在忙，第一片已经开始下一单。

57
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,080
Like a car factory:
就像汽车厂，

58
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,050
lots of cars on the line at once.
流水线上同时好多辆车。

59
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:47,380
A fifty nine station line
一条59站的流水线，

60
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:50,210
serves lots of people's questions at the same time.
同时处理好多人的问题。

61
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:52,850
Count them: twenty four wafers for the big layers,
算一下：24片放大层，

62
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:55,250
thirty five for the light ones. Fifty nine.
35片放小层，正好59。

63
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:57,480
The light layers keep a small fixed notebook,
小层只记一个固定大小的小本子，

64
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,340
so two of them can share one wafer.
所以两层能挤一片。

65
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:01,200
The result: for a model this huge,
结果：这么大的模型，

66
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,060
the target is one to two thousand tokens a second.
目标一秒一千到两千个词元。

67
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:05,590
For comparison: when you read,
对比一下：你读书，

68
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:08,000
you manage maybe four or five words a second.
一秒大约读四五个词。

69
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,290
What it writes in one second
它一秒写的，

70
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:11,200
would take you several minutes to read.
够你读好几分钟。

71
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:13,830
Friendly fine print: this is the company's own blog.
友情提示：这是公司自己的博客，

72
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:16,380
It's a deployment plan, not an independent test.
例子是一份部署方案，还没有第三方实测。

73
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:18,100
And a whole wafer is hard to make.
而且整片晶圆很难造，

74
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,610
It carries spare cores to route around defects.
它得留备用的核，绕开坏点。

75
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:22,250
So the secret isn't just bigger.
所以秘诀不是越大越好，

76
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:24,000
It's stop running to the fridge.
是别再跑冰箱。

77
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,600
Inside computers, moving data
在电脑里，搬数据

78
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,770
often costs more than doing the math.
常常比算数还贵。

79
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:29,800
So next time your AI answers instantly,
下次AI秒回你的时候，

80
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,440
thank the chef who never leaves the kitchen.
谢谢那个从不出厨房的厨师。

